.TH TREE-TRUNK 1 "August 2026" "tree-trunk 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tree-trunk \- TUI and CLI for listing git repos and managing worktrees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tree-trunk
[\fIflags\fR]
.br
.B tree-trunk query
[\fIflags\fR]
.br
.B tree-trunk describe
.br
.B tree-trunk completion
{\fIzsh\fR|\fIbash\fR}
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tree-trunk
finds every git repository on your machine, shows their status at a glance,
and lets you manage git worktrees (create, delete, lock, prune) from one
interactive terminal app.
.PP
It shells out to system
.B git
(>= 2.38); there is no bundled implementation. The interactive TUI is the
default; subcommands provide a deterministic, parseable interface for
scripts and coding agents.
.SH TUI
With no arguments,
.B tree-trunk
launches an interactive terminal app:
.TP
.B Left sidebar
every repo, its branch and change status. \fBj\fR/\fBk\fR move, \fBl\fR expands worktrees.
.TP
.B Main panel
tabs for the selected repo: \fB1\fR status, \fB2\fR worktrees, \fB3\fR history, \fB4\fR diff.
.TP
.B Worktrees
\fBn\fR create, \fBd\fR delete (double-confirmed, never deletes a branch), \fBL\fR lock/unlock, \fBP\fR prune, \fBo\fR copy path.
.TP
.B Diffs
\fBm\fR cycles working/staged/main, \fBp\fR toggles summary, \fBs\fR toggles side-by-side.
.PP
Press \fB?\fR for the full key reference.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS query
Emit the entire repo/worktree/status picture as a single deterministic JSON
document. Answer "what's working where, and how much" for an orchestrator.
.TP
.B \-\-json
pretty JSON (default).
.TP
.B \-\-filter \fIk=v\fR
keep repos matching \fIk=v\fR (repeatable, AND-ed). Keys: id, name, branch,
dirty, prunable, locked, bare, worktrees (count).
.TP
.B \-\-fields \fIa,b\fR
emit only the given top-level fields (repeatable or comma-separated).
.TP
.B \-\-repo \fIPATH\fR
explicit repo path (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-scan-root \fIROOT\fR
scan root (repeatable; replaces defaults).
.TP
.B \-\-no-scan
do not scan; use \-\-repo only.
.PP
Each repo has a stable \fIid\fR (the canonical git dir), its worktrees
(path, branch, is_main, locked, prunable, dirty), and status (branch, ahead,
behind, per-file entries with a porcelain \fIcode\fR).
.SS describe
Print a self-describing JSON schema of this CLI: the subcommands, their
flags, and the output documents. Useful for agents that cannot parse prose
help text.
.SS completion
.B tree-trunk completion zsh
or
.B tree-trunk completion bash
prints a shell completion script for that shell.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tree-trunk/config.toml
optional configuration (scan roots, discovery options, themes).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/tree-trunk/state.json
recently-opened repos.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non-zero on error. (A richer exit-code contract for agents is
planned.)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-worktree (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Aarno Stormborn and contributors.
